@page
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Home";
}
@*
    The home page: https://6093.firstpvrobotics.com/
    Everything below is plain HTML. Change the words between the tags.
    The notes in <!-- --> tell you what goes where; visitors don't see them.
*@

<section class="team-hero">
    <div class="container hero-grid">
        <div>
            <!-- FTC or FRC, your team number, and the year you started. -->
            <span class="eyebrow">FTC Team #6093 · Since 2012</span>
            <!-- Your team's name. -->
            <h1>Deviation From the Norm</h1>
            <!-- One sentence about what your team is about. -->
            <p class="tagline">Gracious Professionalism, awards and robot performance.</p>
            <!-- Short facts shown as bubbles. Add or delete <li> lines. -->
            <ul class="chips">
                <li>Founded 2012, revived 2022</li>
                <li>15 committed members</li>
                <li>Programming help for other FTC teams</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <!-- Your logo, in wwwroot/images/. Use background: #000000 for logos drawn on black. -->
        <div class="hero-logo" style="background: #ffffff">
            <img src="/images/deviation-logo.png" alt="Deviation From the Norm logo" />
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
    <div class="container story">
        <!-- Your team's story. One <p> per paragraph. -->
        <div class="prose">
            <p>Deviation From the Norm formed in 2012 and went dormant before COVID-19 in 2019. Students revived the team in 2022. We strive to embody FIRST's Gracious Professionalism while competing for awards and pushing robot performance. This year 15 members are committed to reaching our goals.</p>
        </div>
        <aside class="card connect">
            <h3>Connect with Deviation</h3>
            <!-- Your team's email address, in both places on the next line. -->
            <p><a href="mailto:deviationftm6093@gmail.com">deviationftm6093@gmail.com</a></p>
            <!-- Links to your team's accounts. -->
            <ul class="pills">
                <li><a href="https://www.instagram.com/deviationfromthenorm" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Instagram</a></li>
                <li><a href="https://www.twitter.com/DeviationFTM" rel="noopener" target="_blank">X</a></li>
            </ul>
        </aside>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- Your outreach projects, one card each. -->
<section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head">
            <span class="eyebrow">Outreach</span>
            <h2>In the community</h2>
            <p class="lede">Some of the ways Deviation shares STEM beyond the competition field.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid grid--3">
            <div class="card item"><h3>Gigi's Playhouse</h3><p class="muted">We partnered with Gigi's Playhouse to give teens with Down syndrome a mini FTC season. Over six weeks, participants built, programmed and showcased their own robots in an inclusive camp.</p></div>
            <div class="card item"><h3>Device Mount</h3><p class="muted">An AEA physical therapist at PV asked for help with a preschool student whose communication device couldn't attach to her stander, so we designed and built a mount for her.</p></div>
            <div class="card item"><h3>Programming Assistance</h3><p class="muted">We fixed a broken Gradle build for team</p></div>
            <div class="card item"><h3>Society of Women Engineers</h3><p class="muted">With 25 female engineers from John Deere, we helped host a SWE event in the PVHS library so young women could learn about careers in engineering and STEM. We made the flyers and sent the invitations.</p></div>
            <div class="card item"><h3>Girl Scouts</h3><p class="muted">At a Girl Scouts camp at Liberty Campground, our members taught young girls about robotics and STEM, helped them code robots and built catapults.</p></div>
            <div class="card item"><h3>FLL Mentoring</h3><p class="muted">Team members go to Pleasant Valley Jr. High to help the FIRST LEGO League team Aquatic Alphas with mechanical design, prototyping and programming.</p></div>
            <div class="card item"><h3>Davenport Public Works</h3><p class="muted">We collected 20 bags of trash to keep it out of the Mississippi River, and we're helping design and install rain gardens around Davenport.</p></div>
            <div class="card item"><h3>Summer Camp</h3><p class="muted">Students in grades 6–8 built and designed robots to compete with their peers, coached by robotics members in programming, 3D modeling and building.</p></div>
            <div class="card item"><h3>Mississippi Valley Fair</h3><p class="muted">We set up a stand at the fair, promoted robotics and FIRST, and let visitors drive our robots.</p></div>
            <div class="card item"><h3>John Deere MTIC</h3><p class="muted">John Deere employees gave us a tour and helped us explore career paths, and we connected with FIRST members and potential mentors.</p></div>
            <div class="card item"><h3>Flags</h3><p class="muted">We set up and take down flags around neighborhoods for patriotic holidays.</p></div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
